<title>CANADA: Torstar Hebdo unit buys stake in ad papers.</title>
<headline>Torstar Hebdo unit buys stake in ad papers.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Torstar Corp said on Monday its 57-percent owned Hebdo Mag Interational Inc unit completed the purchase of controlling interests in the dominant classified advertising publications in Europe for C$75 million.</p>
<p>Torstar said revenues from the purchase of the publications in Italy, Russia, Holland, the Italian part of Switzerland and a small interest in the dominant free ad publisher in the United Kingdom and Ireland, will increase Hebdo Mag's annual revenues to about C$230 million.  </p>
<p>Torstar holds a 50-percent voting interest in Hebdo, which publishes classified advertising magazines and papers in 15 countries in North America, Europe and Asia.</p>
<p>The largest of the publications in the acquisition are &quot;Secondamano&quot; in Northern Italy and the Russian publication &quot;Is Ruk Vruki.&quot;</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
